### 8. 🛡️ Threat Prevention — *"Automated security responses"*

**What it does:** When any module detects a threat, this system **automatically responds** to neutralize it.

**Actions it can take:**

| Threat Level | Automatic Response |
|-------------|-------------------|
| **CRITICAL** | Kill the process + quarantine the file + block domain/IP + alert user |
| **HIGH** | Quarantine the file + block domain + alert user |
| **MEDIUM** | Alert user with recommendation |
| **LOW** | Log the event |

**Specific capabilities:**
- **Kill malicious processes** — Terminates running programs identified as threats
- **Block domains** — Adds malicious websites to the Windows [hosts](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/CGP-2/core/threat_prevention.py#204-238) file to prevent access
- **Block IPs** — Creates Windows Firewall rules to block attacker IP addresses
- **Quarantine files** — Moves infected files to a quarantine vault (encrypted with AES-256 so they can't run)
- **Restore from quarantine** — If a file was a false positive, it can be restored

**Key files:** [threat_prevention.py](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/CGP-2/core/threat_prevention.py), [quarantine.py](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/CGP-2/core/quarantine.py)

